#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087687 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087434 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5bf8c8b-64f1-5552-a59e-78eef021c122" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Lines Given in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "b2f31785-e173-518c-a1fd-b069e0834b2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-14367" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is parallel to $12x - y=3$?\n\n1. $y=4x-8$\n2. $y=12x+1$\n3. $y=3x-12$" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $12x-y=3$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x - y &= 3 \\\\\n- y &= -12x + 3 \\\\\ny &= 12x - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $12$.\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $12$ is\n\n$$\ny = 12x+1\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5bf8c8b-64f1-5552-a59e-78eef021c122" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049201}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5bf8c8b-64f1-5552-a59e-78eef021c122" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Lines Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6bf01d9-1387-514b-afb5-fde88dafcb9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{3}{2}x + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084615} {:answer/id #uuid "1e7fa38f-3d7a-58ce-b27f-e3d665aba389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{9}{4}x + \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084616} {:answer/id #uuid "25180595-bbf1-583a-9a44-97d13f692586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 6x + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084617} {:answer/id #uuid "38aee078-8100-5d7d-9eb6-406ce83f2e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{3}x -